- git plugin
	- large git diffs are slow to load and scroll
	- add default commit message to settings, replace the 1 file commit message with it if set. Otherwise, use placeholder.
	- make the placeholder actually work if you press commit, however it should still act as a placeholder (ie. does not need to be deleted to write a custom message)
	- placeholder should work for up to 5 files, comma delimited
	- put status bar info in panel as well, alongside the path a the top.
	- divider between staged / unstaged to seperate them a bit more
	
- ui cleanup
	- use shared functions for ui
		- ui audit for duplicated style building
			- we've found large performance issues with duplicate menu style building and other things
		- consistent dialog styling and sizing
			- dialogs often appear uncentered in the window and with a size that is way too small. can we abstract this behind some kind of helper function?

- terminal
	- Make terminal closing asynchronous. Signal the worker to stop, remove the terminal from the UI immediately, and let the worker finish process cleanup independently. Keep a way to reap finished workers without blocking a frame. This addresses the confirmed 500 ms per-terminal stall.
	- Stop hidden output from invalidating the window. Continue processing output on the worker, but request snapshots and trigger redraws only for visible terminals. Refresh a snapshot when a terminal becomes visible. Track title changes and process exits separately so background tabs still update correctly.

- performance
	- investigate shader effect performance
	
